{"id":"8fa3940b26f1c35b2d99e96a3846c248752a08aecd2b133c5685bbf4b77f81ad","at":"2026-10-06T05:33:44Z","commit":"4e603ba081e9d6f23de3cbf3bf7b1bb3c60b1f82","parents":[],"op":"retire","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"ExTLA.Spec","hash":"df10c014"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/04-layer2-model-checker.md#Layer 2: Specification DSL + Model Checker/Overview","hash":"a3277a45"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Declined (#352): the Overview names ExTLA.Spec as one of Layer 2's four components. The DSL has its own sections (Overview/DSL Macro Reference, Module: ExTLA.Spec.Compiled), which carry its implementation relations. The Overview's own claims are the three DSL rules, held by its verifies-tagged tests."}
{"id":"eeeab4271d92e3e85c7a8dc7d83e84fb20813895862fe7a57b8933e443cf77b7","at":"2026-10-06T05:33:50Z","commit":"4e603ba081e9d6f23de3cbf3bf7b1bb3c60b1f82","parents":[],"op":"retire","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"ExTLA.ModelChecker","hash":"bed18c77"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/04-layer2-model-checker.md#Layer 2: Specification DSL + Model Checker/Overview","hash":"a3277a45"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Declined (#352): the Overview names ExTLA.ModelChecker as one of Layer 2's components. Its behaviour is specified, and related, under Module: ExTLA.ModelChecker and its API, State Graph, Safety and Liveness sections. The Overview's own claims are the three DSL rules, which the checker consumes but does not implement."}
{"id":"0c49b5149e16115672ea0f91a9f829b39a7455acc039280092f3ae3a2fdeb830","at":"2026-10-06T05:33:54Z","commit":"4e603ba081e9d6f23de3cbf3bf7b1bb3c60b1f82","parents":[],"op":"retire","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"ExTLA.Trace","hash":"cab0c0c2"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/04-layer2-model-checker.md#Layer 2: Specification DSL + Model Checker/Overview","hash":"a3277a45"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Declined (#352): the Overview lists ExTLA.Trace (counterexample generation) as a component. Its behaviour is specified under Module: ExTLA.Trace, which relates it (#353's half). Nothing in the Overview's own text is a claim about Trace's behaviour."}
{"id":"6ef3f4574e71bf5ad3f07905a3c2344d4f70880fb591075ea1ec137e08ef8852","at":"2026-10-06T05:33:57Z","commit":"4e603ba081e9d6f23de3cbf3bf7b1bb3c60b1f82","parents":[],"op":"retire","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"ExTLA.Coverage","hash":"aabf0d8f"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/04-layer2-model-checker.md#Layer 2: Specification DSL + Model Checker/Overview","hash":"a3277a45"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Declined (#352): the Overview lists ExTLA.Coverage ('what the run actually exercised') as a component. Its behaviour is specified under Coverage and Vacuity, which relates it (#353's half). Nothing in the Overview's own text is a claim about Coverage's behaviour."}
{"id":"a8f06ba81156bec5a96b305a8ef239c6c38d751386c8feade547ea19786bb217","at":"2026-10-06T06:02:28Z","commit":"792e339b44bfd56207068dd81799d52d15874727","parents":[],"op":"retire","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"ExTLA.Coverage","hash":"aabf0d8f"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/04-layer2-model-checker.md#Layer 2: Specification DSL + Model Checker/Per-declaration cost — `ExTLA.Profile`","hash":"3c942c72"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Declined (#353): the section's first line contrasts Profile with Coverage ('Coverage answers how often the checker asked a declaration; Profile answers what the answer cost'). Coverage implements §Coverage and Vacuity, not this section."}
{"id":"74d672b2c6a2de18717b492042c223e7e05cb706da5733ed717d5f84570f2027","at":"2026-10-06T06:02:31Z","commit":"792e339b44bfd56207068dd81799d52d15874727","parents":[],"op":"retire","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"ExTLA.Spec.Compiled","hash":"93195230"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/04-layer2-model-checker.md#Layer 2: Specification DSL + Model Checker/Per-declaration cost — `ExTLA.Profile`","hash":"3c942c72"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Declined (#353): Spec.Compiled is cited as the holder of the closures that Profile.instrument/1 wraps. The wrapping, and 'an unprofiled run pays nothing', are Profile's behaviour (profile_test: 'an unprofiled run leaves the compiled spec's own closures in place'). Compiled implements its own section."}
{"id":"382c87b2ce66e704543db63ab00be6e2ca98c21fb7e5c1c283100ef83b4963c3","at":"2026-10-06T06:02:36Z","commit":"792e339b44bfd56207068dd81799d52d15874727","parents":[],"op":"retire","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"ExTLA.Coverage.merge/2","hash":"e9b910ac"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/04-layer2-model-checker.md#Layer 2: Specification DSL + Model Checker/Per-declaration cost — `ExTLA.Profile`/Under `--workers`","hash":"e451e4e8"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Declined (#353): Coverage.merge/2 is cited as the analogue ('sums them beside ExTLA.Coverage.merge/2'). The per-worker profile summing this section specifies is Parallel's private merge/2 and Profile's own merge, kept via the Parallel relation. Coverage.merge/2 combines coverage, not profiles."}
{"id":"30be294ca263653c75bb6a46a61ec43ee90d4f3b0a907921437217f0ef78128d","at":"2026-10-06T06:02:40Z","commit":"792e339b44bfd56207068dd81799d52d15874727","parents":[],"op":"retire","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"ExTLA.Spec.Block","hash":"ddf5f370"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/04-layer2-model-checker.md#Layer 2: Specification DSL + Model Checker/Per-declaration cost — `ExTLA.Profile`/Example profile output","hash":"a147ac5a"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Declined (#353): Spec.Block is named only in the closing paragraph, as where deferred sub-expression attribution would need a compile-time transform. It describes work not done, so nothing implements it. The example output itself is Profile.format's."}
{"id":"314b488d031be08aee46e5e5fa6311994e60268a9809e882537396da0c78e6d0","at":"2026-10-06T06:02:43Z","commit":"792e339b44bfd56207068dd81799d52d15874727","parents":[],"op":"retire","type":"implements","ends":[{"kind":"code","id":"ExTLA.State","hash":"ef4ce22c"},{"kind":"spec","id":"spec/04-layer2-model-checker.md#Layer 2: Specification DSL + Model Checker/Module: `ExTLA.Trace`/Exploring a trace","hash":"61849bb0"}],"by":"Doug ClymerOlson <doug@yarina.org>","note":"Declined (#353): an aside, 'A ExTLA.State.t() is a plain map'. It is read as the module through the type-citation stopgap (surfex#137). It explains why explore/3 needs no Trace Explorer apparatus; State implements nothing this section specifies. Trace.explore/3 does, kept."}
